{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa Breaks Up With Marco"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Trying to Work It Out"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 12}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le12ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Making and Responding to Promises"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you make a promise to someone, you tell them that you will definitely do something in the future. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">will</span> to make promises. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I'll never behave like that again.<br> I promise I'll talk to you about it next time. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I'll never behave like that again. I promise I'll talk to you about it next time. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ok. <br>Sounds good.<br> I hope so!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ben</span>: I'll always talk to you about my problems."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Becca</span>: I hope so! I promise I'll listen."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Possible Actions in the Future"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future tense (<span class=\"strong\">will</span>) to talk about actions in the future. You can also use the modals <span class=\"strong\">might</span> and <span class=\"strong\">may</span> to talk about possible actions in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">will </span> goes before the verb. The short form is \u2018ll. The negative form is will not of <span class=\"strong\">  won't</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the Future tense when you talk about the future, make offers or make predictions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The modals <span class=\"strong\">might</span> and <span class=\"strong\">may</span> go before the verb. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "They talk about future possibility or chance that something will happen. <br><span class=\"strong\">Might </span>means there is a smaller chance that something will happen (30%).<br><span class=\"strong\">May </span> means there is a slightly greater chance that something will happen (50%)."}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Petra</span>: Will you come with me?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Kevin</span>: Hmm..I may be working on the weekend. I'll let you know later today. "}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to act"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to do something in a particular way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I never act like that. I don't know what happened."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le12ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to make promises."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to behave"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to act in a particular way "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I won't behave like that again."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le12ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to bottle things up inside "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to keep your feelings inside and not talk about them"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: It's not good to bottle things up inside."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le12ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to deserve something "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to behave in a way that is worthy of reward "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(ve